// Module `dir`: directories below a Dir, the capability for one directory tree (CAP-1,
// CAP-2, CAP-7). Dir is a core capability type, plain and `send`; copying it copies the
// designation. A run's Dirs come from `main`'s granted parameters (CAP-4) and from
// `create_temp`. Paths are Strings resolved relative to their Dir, which they may not
// leave (core.md); the seed has no Path type. Every operation is library code over one
// host primitive, passes the replay point at issue and at delivery (CAP-8) and, being
// `waits`, is a cancellation point (CONC-7). Field legend: API.md; "Prefix:" says what has
// happened on the host when the operation fails or is cancelled part way. No operation
// here admits anything (core.md, "Host").
//
// Left out: `narrow` (a Dir for a subdirectory). core.md has no host primitive that
// returns a Dir for an existing directory, only `host.mkdtemp`.
/// Creates the directory p; its parent must exist. `host.mkdir`.
/// Fails: Error(Exists | NotFound | Denied | Other(_)).
/// Prefix: on failure nothing was created; a cancellation observed at delivery leaves the
/// directory created. Ex: `std.dir.create_dir(d, "tmp")?`
pub fn create_dir(d: Dir, p: String) -> Result[(), IoError] waits {
    host.mkdir(d, p)
}

/// Removes p and everything below it, depth first. `host.remove_tree`.
/// Fails: Error(NotFound | Denied | Other(_)) at the first entry that cannot be removed.
/// Prefix: entries removed before the failure stay removed; not atomic.
/// Ex: `std.dir.remove_all(d, "tmp")?`
pub fn remove_all(d: Dir, p: String) -> Result[(), IoError] waits {
    host.remove_tree(d, p)
}

/// Creates a new empty directory with a fresh name directly below d, appends that name (at
/// most 32 ASCII bytes) to `name` and returns a Dir for it (Go os.MkdirTemp).
/// `host.mkdtemp`: the name lands in capacity the caller already holds, so `name` needs 32
/// bytes of spare capacity. It is not removed automatically: `dir.remove_all(d, name)`
/// removes it and everything below it.
/// Fails: Bounds (failure), checked before issue, when name has less than 32 bytes spare;
/// Error(Denied | Other(_)), name unchanged. Prefix: on failure nothing was created; a
/// cancellation observed at delivery leaves the directory created and name unchanged.
/// Ex: `let mut name = string.with_capacity(32)?; let tmp = std.dir.create_temp(d, mut name)?; ..; std.dir.remove_all(d, name)?`
pub fn create_temp(d: Dir, mut name: String) -> Result[Dir, IoError] waits {
    host.mkdtemp(d, mut name)
}
